+# PR621 reset-resume and expected-deferral clarification — 2026-11-21
+
+- Normal reset commits `accountReset.state:done` in R2 BEFORE its awaited promise resolves; resolver denial applies only during `running`. R1 atomically creates admin-readable `portalAccountReconciliation/{patientId}` with `state:reset_in_progress`, `resumeAvailable:true` and a 60-second `reviewAfterMs` deadline. A crash after R1 cannot omit that signal. Operators inspect overdue entries; no new scheduler or automatic fence stealing is added. R2 resolves the entry synchronously.
+- Existing authenticated `adminIssueInvite` accepts `resumeReset:true` with explicit `elationPatientId` and `actor` (optional audit reason). This is reset-only: it resumes the SAME exact UID/owner/generation with all existing quiescence and suppression checks, returns `{ok:true,resetState:"done"}`, and exits BEFORE revoke/remint/send code. Already-done resume is a no-op even if a successor has claimed. It does not clear unknown work or bypass RESET_BUSY. Example owner/backend payload: `{"elationPatientId":"<patient ID from reset queue>","actor":"<operator>","resumeReset":true,"reason":"resume interrupted reset"}`. Call through existing authenticated admin transport, not a public browser request. Missing reset fails closed.
+- Double-submit losers re-read the patient's exact, consistent binding. Completed setup returns clean 409 `ALREADY_CLAIMED` / sign in without reconciliation. A known fresh claim still in progress returns 409 `CLAIM_IN_PROGRESS`, also without reconciliation; stale, unreadable or durably uncertain ownership keeps generic support/hold semantics. Auth transport uncertainty is recorded on the existing ownership document BEFORE returning, so it cannot masquerade as benign concurrency.
+- Expected soft-budget deferral writes deferred + Recovery queue, then joins actual hydration inside the current awaited invocation with a bounded drain (default up to 30 seconds, capped for invocation headroom). If underlying work actually settles and no nested mutation deadline occurred, release owner with NO reconciliation; Recovery can take the deferred patient. A drain that cannot establish quiescence or a nested non-cancelling mutation deadline remains a genuine anomaly, retains ownership, and emits reconciliation. No detached release or clock-based takeover; the existing scheduled Recovery decision helper is unchanged.
+- Social status read-only on 2026-11-21: production master `config/socialSignIn.enabled=false`; default practice gate=true; five social callables deployed ACTIVE. Thus deployed but OFF for users. No provider, practice, master, registration or runtime settings changed. Full social gate includes nonce/no-mutation/deploy units, Auth+Firestore+Functions callable flows and lifecycle fence/generation tests; Elation/Twilio/provider identities remain synthetic adapters in these emulator tests.
+- Full hydration gate still executes modified worker units, queue/Recovery/drain units, existing C4/rules suites AND lifecycle emulator tests; workflow name, behavior and docs-only predicate unchanged. `adminRevokeInvite`, claim token service and claimAccount consumption block remain unchanged by this follow-up. #619 is separate after PR1 merge. No merge/deploy/arming/live reset or send.
+
+# Claim reset/adoption security amendment — 2026-11-21 (Closes #617, Closes #618)
+
+- `adminIssueInvite(resetClaim:true)` resolves by patient ID, deletes only the verified true-case `authUid`, disables/revokes refresh tokens and confirms exact Auth absence before clearing binding. Legacy email lookup discovers only a candidate; unique roster email, matching normalized stored binding, unique patient ownership and independent patient-ID `member_bound` evidence are mandatory. Shared/unknown/conflicting legacy identity holds for reconciliation. Privileged/unexpected provider identities hold rather than being deleted.
+- Reset R1 transaction serializes with patient `accountWork` ownership and active patient-specific hydration run/job state, retaining both UID fields. `RESET_BUSY` returns 409 with an operator-visible explanation and reconciliation signal. Any delete/revoke/confirmation uncertainty retains reset fence and binding, returns an error, and never remints/sends. Retry continues the same exact-UID reset operation.
+- Reset R2 transaction rechecks operation, generation, bindings and quiescence; deletes only this patient's old-UID job, revokes its tokens, removes only its unowned pending/queued recovery entries and clears UID/claim/identity hydration residue. Preserves chart/storage identity, cached records, guardian relationships, portal controls and verified complete hydration. Increments identity generation; retains audit history. No global run or patient cleanup.
+- `claimAccount` never treats `email-already-exists` as ownership. Existing-account recovery requires exact patient `authUid` or current-generation server-written `claimAccountIntent` (pre-generated valid Firebase UID persisted before create). Exact/normalized patient binding uniqueness and patient-only Auth identity are checked. Unknown ownership returns one generic 503 `SETUP_REVIEW_REQUIRED` / contact-support message, with no account identity/collision reason. Server writes patient-ID-only `portalAccountReconciliation` plus `portalAdminAudit`; queue is admin-read/client-write-denied.
+- Account intent is provenance, NOT token reservation (#619 remains separate). No passwords/raw invite/session tokens persisted. Uncertain bind outcome never rollback-deletes a possible winner; proof remains available. Proven credential failure records an incomplete checkpoint permitting only the same identity's recovery, not completed-account password overwrite.
+- Patient-scoped `accountWork` is owner/generation checked and never stolen solely because a lease expired. Reset rejects running/unknown work; unknown process termination requires reconciliation. Soft-budget hydration retains ownership while the underlying backfill can still write, emitting a visible hold if completion cannot be acknowledged. Normal successful work releases ownership. Worker compares triggering job incarnation with current job before acquisition/success/error writes and never recreates or overwrites a replacement.
+- Core record resolver denies a reset-in-progress binding. Refresh revocation/deletion does not promise immediate universal logout; issued ID tokens/signed URLs may outlive deletion, binding removal is the core real-time enforcement. No project-wide session kill or post-grant undo.
+- `adminRevokeInvite` source/signature/audit/error behavior, suppression-first invite checks, #615 age gate, discovery/AUTOSEND, wave/config gates and schedules are unchanged. #619 consumption/reservation remains untouched until a separate PR after this merges; C2 is its future grant authorization boundary.
+- `claim-hydration-gate` keeps its workflow/job name and #611/#613 docs-only no-op-pass predicate byte unchanged. Adds a separately isolated Auth+Firestore lifecycle suite after all existing units/rules/C4 suites. Emulator coverage is not hosted session-revocation or real Elation/SendGrid certification. No merge/deploy/arming/production cleanup authorized.
+
+## Read-only legacy-binding count and backfill proposal
+
+- At 2026-11-21T15:20:47Z, 1,625 patient documents read: **0** with nonempty `firebaseUid` and missing/empty `authUid`; **0** unique-email and **0** shared/missing-email candidates. No backfill required or executed.
+- If a future audited export finds legacy rows: propose an owner-approved, dry-run-default, explicit patient-ID list backfill. Unique normalized roster email is only a candidate filter, not identity proof. Require exact Auth candidate normalized to the stored UID, independent patient-ID binding evidence, no duplicate exact/normalized patient ownership, no reset/work fence and no conflicting provider/privilege. Re-read evidence and unchanged binding in a transaction; set ONLY missing `authUid`, with audit. Never change firebaseUid/credentials/claim/hydration or send. Shared emails, absent proof and read uncertainty remain manual. Applying this proposal needs separate production-write approval.
